itatively ('bounded retry window', '20-25 seconds' replication lag) but never fixed as a concrete default — max attempts, interval/backoff, and total timeout ceiling are unstated, yet an AC verifies behavior 'within the retry budget'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f723825ea2af06b44","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('bounded retry window') and AC 'A fetch that cannot reach the target within the retry budget produces no signature'","norm_id":"nc71a2d1dce0f313b","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor picks a total timeout shorter than 25s and gates flap on legitimate post-merge lag","Test for the lag-wait AC cannot be written deterministically without a defined attempt schedule"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a default such as: 'fetch retried every 5s up to a 60s ceiling (≥ observed 20-25s lag plus margin); exhaustion is a refusal.' Reference this constant in the retry-budget ACs.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the workspace refresh and the gate's pinned HEAD resolution occur under a single continuously-held checkout lock (or otherwise state the atomicity guarantee) so a concurrent refresh/warm-up cannot move HEAD between the freshness boundary and the resolve.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: helper does 'take the existing checkout lock, require a clean tree, git fetch origin main, then git merge --ff-only origin/main' and is 'Invoke[d] ... before a certified gate resolves a HEAD-based attested ref'","transition_close.py:140-142 pins resolve_ref('HEAD', root, fetch=False) as a separate step from any refresh","cache.py:207 acquire() reads via resolve_ref on the same repo_root; the refresh mutates that same working tree via ff-only merge","Entrypoint warm-up refresh (plan Scope) can run concurrently against the same MCP_CODE_DIR volume"],"finding":"The refresh helper is specified to take the checkout lock internally and is then invoked 'before' the gate resolves the ref, but the plan does not require the refresh and the subsequent pinned HEAD-resolution to occur under a single continuously-held lock. Because the shared checkout is mutated by git merge --ff-only and read by the attested resolve path (resolve_ref/acquire with fetch=False on the same repo_root), a concurrent refresh from another gate or the entrypoint warm-up could advance or mid-merge HEAD in the window between the helper releasing the lock and the gate resolving HEAD, reintroducing a check-then-act gap on a signing-correctness boundary.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f142ec6eef2b46550","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section — 'take the existing checkout lock ... Invoke it as a freshness boundary before a certified gate resolves a HEAD-based attested ref'","norm_id":"nc2e9e8033a9e6bc2","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two gate operations (or a gate plus the entrypoint warm-up) run against the same gerrit_mcp_code volume; one advances HEAD after the other's refresh released the lock but before it pinned HEAD","A gate pins HEAD mid-merge if the resolve is not serialized with the refresh's lock hold"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have the refresh helper return (or the gate seam hold) the checkout lock across both the ff-only advance and the pinned resolve_ref('HEAD', fetch=False), releasing only after the SHA is pinned; add an acceptance criterion asserting a concurrent refresh cannot change the resolved SHA between boundary and pin.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly whether claim-time currency (`current_head_sha` with `fetch=False`) is fixed by this unit or deferred, adding it to Scope or Out of scope with a one-line rationale.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3637,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Claim-time currency is not protected: current_head_sha resolves with fetch=False (gate_source.py:89-109), comparing against a local idea of origin/main.'","Out-of-scope lists 'Mode A snapshot resolution, which already fetches' but does not name the claim-time currency (`current_head_sha`) path."],"finding":"The plan identifies a second staleness surface — claim-time currency via `current_head_sha` resolving with `fetch=False` (gate_source.py:89-109) — and states it is 'not protected,' but does not explicitly place it in scope or in the Out-of-scope section, leaving its disposition ambiguous relative to the title's promise that gates no longer verify a stale tree.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fba7d6b10d077f3b1","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Why it is a signing-correctness hole' / Out of scope","norm_id":"n4f3b0611991e9b9a","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer reading the plan cannot tell whether claim-time freshness is a deliberate non-goal or an oversight; a claim gate could still resolve currency against a stale local `origin/main` after this ships."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a line to Out of scope: 'Claim-time currency (`current_head_sha`, gate_source.py:89-109) — the HEAD-based attested-ref boundary is this unit's correctness surface; currency freshening is deferred to a follow-up,' or bring it into scope.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the replication-lag retry window reuses the existing `REBAR_SNAPSHOT_STALL_ATTEMPTS`/`fetch_origin` retry seam (extending it to cover a not-yet-present target ref) or introduces a new knob/loop, and justify any new config surface against the existing one.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.481,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The codebase already exposes a fetch retry budget: `resolve_stall_attempts` reading `REBAR_SNAPSHOT_STALL_ATTEMPTS` (src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:47-50), driving the attempt loop in `fetch_origin` (src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py:286-288).","That existing loop retries ONLY transient stalls/CAS ('Retry transient stalls only, with a bounded attempt count', git_fetch.py:224); a MISSING target ref is NOT retried — it surfaces as a resolution error (`resolve_ref` swallows `is_missing_ref` and raises `SnapshotRefError`, src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:211-230). So the plan's replication-lag 'wait for a not-yet-present SHA' is a distinct retry class the current budget does not serve.","The plan calls the retry window 'bounded' but names no config source, no default, and no relationship to the existing `REBAR_SNAPSHOT_STALL_*` knobs — leaving open whether it adds a new knob or a new loop."],"finding":"The plan's 'bounded retry window' for replication lag does not state whether it reuses the existing fetch-retry budget/seam or introduces a new retry loop and config knob, risking config-surface proliferation or a duplicate retry loop.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb4c54e4fd32554c6","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section ('The fetch needs a bounded retry window ... 20-25 seconds') and AC 'A target SHA appearing only after replication lag is waited for'","norm_id":"nac13e4b660068496","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds a new REBAR_* attempts/timeout env var beside the existing stall knobs, proliferating the config surface for a near-identical concept.","Implementer writes a fresh retry+backoff loop instead of extending the existing `fetch_origin` attempt seam, duplicating retry machinery."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the retry-budget ceiling against replication-lag headroom (e.g. p99 or a stated safety multiple of the 20-25s observation), not the observed minimum.","cohor